-- Prince George's County deterministic rule pack — migrated from the retired
-- hardcoded princeGeorgesCountyRulePack TypeScript evaluator into data-driven
-- CHECK rows. Generated from packages/compliance/src/prince-georges-rule-data.ts
-- (the same data the Phase 0/3 parity tests assert against) — not hand-transcribed,
-- so there is no drift between what's tested and what ships.
--
-- Not migrated (see packages/compliance/src/rule-engine.ts module doc):
-- PG_PROFESSIONAL_RELEASE, PG_SIGNED_SEALED_PLOT_PLAN — both are "does a seal exist"
-- checks, superseded by evaluateProfessionalRelease / submitSitePlanToJurisdiction,
-- which check the real ProfessionalReviewRecord instead of a jurisdiction CHECK row.
--
-- Applied by hand via `prisma db execute` (see 20260730162359_site_plan_rule_engine_relations
-- for why `prisma migrate dev` cannot run against this database), then verified via the
-- live-DB parity test in prince-georges-seed-parity.integration.test.ts, then marked applied.

